PARITY NOTES (web WidgetStatusGrid.tsx -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- States: the web source is a PURE presentational primitive (no data hooks). It has exactly two render
  branches, both reproduced: empty (cells.length===0 -> EmptyState, mapped to TsEmptyState) and the
  populated responsive grid of ok/warning/error/inactive/unknown chips with a corner status dot. The generic
  loading/error/stale/offline fetch states do not exist in the source and are intentionally NOT fabricated
  (per honesty covenant #2/#3) — they belong to the data-bound widgets that consume this primitive.
- statusStyles (web L21-L42) -> WidgetStatusPalette: ok/warning/error are tinted semantic accents
  (Success/Warning/Danger brushes at /10 background + /20 border); inactive/unknown share the neutral
  muted-surface treatment (SurfaceGlass bg, Border border, TextMuted dot).
- Container-query column collapse (web L44-L50, cols 2|3|4 + compact, @xs=320 / @sm=384) is reproduced by
  WidgetStatusGridLayout.ResolveColumns and applied on the view's measured width (WinUI has no container
  queries). Verified by unit tests at every breakpoint.
- compact hides per-cell values (web L92) and forces two columns (web L63).
- i18n (P1/S10): the web default emptyMessage ('No status data available') is a hard-coded prop default with
  NO dedicated catalog key. The primitive resolves its fallback through the shared generic catalog key
  translation.common.noData ("No data available", present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw); consuming
  widgets pass their own specific localized message. No English literal is rendered without the facade.
- a11y: every chip exposes a Narrator name (label, plus value when shown); the status dot and inner texts are
  marked decorative (AccessibilityView.Raw) so the chip is a single clean Narrator stop — matching the web
  (colour-only dot, no aria text alternative). Verified by the a11y-name tests.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): view.opened slug=WidgetStatusGrid is emitted once on Loaded via
  WidgetStatusGridDiagnostics. Verified by unit test.

